## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical use of Blob Storage for per-tenant isolation, TTL-based data retention, and a lightweight CI/CD approach.

## Key Concepts

- HTTP-triggered Azure Functions and streaming uploads
- Azure Blob Storage per-tenant isolation
- Azure App Configuration for per-tenant TTL
- Timer-triggered background cleanup
- Basic end-to-end tests and environment promotion via GitHub Actions

## Code Example

```javascript
// Upload handler sketch
import { BlobServiceClient } from '@azure/storage-blob';
module.exports = async function (context, req) {
  const tenant = req.headers['tenantid'];
  const file = req.body; // multipart parsed in real impl
  const container = client.getContainerClient(tenant);
  await container.createIfNotExists();
  const blob = container.getBlockBlobClient(file.name);
